message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: 'Code for "All Bell inequalities with a quantum advantage in the minimal scenario are self-testing"'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code for the paper "All Bell inequalities with a quantum advantage in the minimal scenario are self-testing".
  The Mathematica notebooks derive the plane of candidate Bell functionals, prove the vertex table of the local
  polygon exactly and verify the six sum-of-squares certificates exactly. The Python scripts compute the NPA
  bounds of Table II and draw Figures 2, 3 and 4.
keywords:
  - Bell inequalities
  - self-testing
  - quantum correlations
  - CHSH
  - sum of squares
  - NPA hierarchy
